0003 — pending-work counters: read-only counts of every queue the frame pump
drains, published as `globalThis.__pocketPendingWork`, so a host can ask
what a mounted app still holds without counting native ops.

Rebased onto 66caf4e5 (2026-10-22). At e0b37e2 the pump drained five
registries; main drains eleven, and `pendingWork()` claims "all zero" about
whatever it reads, so each of the six new ones is counted: the system
layer's frame registry (`SystemFrameContext`, which runs while the app is
suspended), live model tasks, model deliveries and queued model commands
(`model-tasks.ts`), native animations a model task awaits
(`model-animation.ts`), model regions written and not yet reacted
(`model-reactive.ts`), and lifecycle hooks registered or destroyed and not
yet flushed (`aot-lifecycle.ts`). `tests/pending-work.test.ts` drives each
through the real frame pump, and each case is red with its counter removed
from `pendingWork()`.

